<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aragonese Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1284–1285</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Sicilian Vespers</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aragonese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was a crusade declared by Pope Martin IV against King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-aragon">Peter III of Aragon</a>, who had taken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Sicilian Vespers</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iii-of-france">Philip III of France</a> invaded Catalonia in 1285 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a>, but disease and the destruction of his fleet by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-of-lauria">Roger of Lauria</a> forced a retreat, and Philip died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perpignan">Perpignan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aragonese-crusade.jpg" alt="Aragonese Crusade" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Setge-girona-1285.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
